1
00:00:00,570 --> 00:00:02,970
Clearly, the position of the chairman and the

2
00:00:02,970 --> 00:00:05,570
MD should be separate, and this separation is

3
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:08,210
not just on paper, but should be actual.

4
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:11,970
In situations where you have a chairman who

5
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:17,230
is also perhaps signing checks or approving matters

6
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:20,190
reserved for management, it does not speak well

7
00:00:20,190 --> 00:00:22,170
of this expected separation.

8
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:26,650
Availability for board responsibilities is also a major

9
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:29,410
feature of the composition and structure of the

10
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:29,650
board.

11
00:00:30,090 --> 00:00:34,330
So whilst boards sometimes look out for heavyweights,

12
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:37,570
for want of a better expression, to appoint

13
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:42,030
to the board, one principal criteria should be

14
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:45,210
how available are these directors to properly discharge

15
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:47,450
their duties and responsibilities to the board.

16
00:00:47,450 --> 00:00:50,850
And so there is a concern around being

17
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:51,590
overboarded.

18
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:56,170
So you have directors appointing multiple board seats,

19
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:58,670
accepting to sit on multiple boards at the

20
00:00:58,670 --> 00:00:59,250
same time.

21
00:00:59,670 --> 00:01:02,570
So boards are reminded to manage the number

22
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:05,510
of directors, the number of other boards that

23
00:01:05,510 --> 00:01:06,710
their directors sit on.

24
00:01:06,710 --> 00:01:11,250
So for instance, the CAMA 2020 has restricted

25
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:15,070
the number of public companies that a director

26
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:16,830
can sit on to five.

27
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:19,930
So you can't be a director of more

28
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:22,010
than five public company boards at the same

29
00:01:22,010 --> 00:01:22,350
time.

30
00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:25,770
The restriction does not apply to private company

31
00:01:25,770 --> 00:01:26,070
boards.

32
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:29,750
However, each board is expected to define how

33
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:34,070
many other boards a director on their board

34
00:01:34,070 --> 00:01:37,170
should sit on, essentially just to help ensure

35
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:40,610
that the directors are available and committed to

36
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:42,630
the board on which he or she is

37
00:01:42,630 --> 00:01:42,930
sitting.

38
00:01:43,570 --> 00:01:45,410
So another aspect of the structure of the

39
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:47,430
board is that the board should have an

40
00:01:47,430 --> 00:01:48,850
effective committee system.

41
00:01:49,390 --> 00:01:51,130
And the code recommends that there should be

42
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:54,770
at least an audit committee, a governance and

43
00:01:54,770 --> 00:01:57,230
remuneration committee, risk management committee.

44
00:01:57,230 --> 00:02:00,230
And this committee should also have charters or

45
00:02:00,230 --> 00:02:04,150
terms of reference that define their mandates, composition,

46
00:02:04,690 --> 00:02:08,690
tenure and frequency of review of those charters.

47
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:12,250
Another element of board effectiveness is the effective

48
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:13,710
use of board committees.

49
00:02:14,490 --> 00:02:17,310
Board committees typically are responsible for drilling down

50
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:21,490
on specific issues, forming an opinion on such

51
00:02:21,490 --> 00:02:25,110
issues and making recommendations to the board.

52
00:02:25,110 --> 00:02:27,450
And to be effective, the committees themselves should

53
00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:30,170
have committee charters that set out the purpose,

54
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:33,190
the composition, the authority and the tenure of

55
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:34,070
committee members.

56
00:02:34,590 --> 00:02:36,030
They should have effective chairs.

57
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:38,530
So the board should, in fact, the board

58
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:41,130
typically or the chairman in some cases, the

59
00:02:41,130 --> 00:02:44,350
one that appoints committee chairs, and such chairs

60
00:02:44,350 --> 00:02:46,630
should be available to have the strength of

61
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:50,590
character and should have the relevant skills to

62
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:52,630
gain the confidence of their peers.

63
00:02:53,370 --> 00:02:55,770
Committees are accountable to the board.

64
00:02:55,990 --> 00:02:59,130
So while committees can deliberate on issues, all

65
00:02:59,130 --> 00:03:00,410
they can do at the end of the

66
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:03,330
day is to make recommendations to the board.

67
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:06,330
Committees are not expected to bind the board

68
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:09,190
or the company with regards to decisions that

69
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:09,670
they take.

70
00:03:10,330 --> 00:03:13,150
They should have access to information and they

71
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:15,910
should have access to training and development.

72
00:03:18,430 --> 00:03:20,810
Another key element of board effectiveness is, of

73
00:03:20,810 --> 00:03:22,090
course, board dynamics.

74
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:25,510
This is how directors interact with one another

75
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:29,290
and how they essentially behave as directors.

76
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:32,350
Individuals come to the board with their egos

77
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:35,570
and their own self-awareness or lack thereof.

78
00:03:36,270 --> 00:03:38,170
All of this can impact how the board

79
00:03:38,170 --> 00:03:41,490
or directors interact or take decisions.

80
00:03:42,030 --> 00:03:45,750
So the language, emotional intelligence, all of this

81
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:48,690
go towards constructive debates or otherwise on the

82
00:03:48,690 --> 00:03:48,950
board.

83
00:03:48,950 --> 00:03:53,250
And so it impacts also the quality of

84
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:54,150
board decisions.

85
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:56,990
So what are some of the individual attributes

86
00:03:56,990 --> 00:04:01,370
of a director that can promote board dynamics?

87
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:04,050
Such a director will work well with others,

88
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:07,550
can disagree but should not be disagreeable, will

89
00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:11,110
possess the required business or industry knowledge, prepares

90
00:04:11,110 --> 00:04:14,470
for and attends meetings punctually and regularly.

91
00:04:14,470 --> 00:04:17,570
There's nothing as instructive to a board as

92
00:04:17,570 --> 00:04:21,170
a director who attends meetings without preparing, reading

93
00:04:21,170 --> 00:04:24,430
through their board papers or doing the required

94
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,470
research ahead of board meetings.

95
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:32,170
Directors should contribute quality conversations to the board

96
00:04:32,170 --> 00:04:35,130
and to the affairs of the business.
